# ---- GOLDEN FIXTURE (bridge tile) ----
# resetMode=loadvm -> restore the INTERNAL 'golden' snapshot: X (-nocursor) +
# VICE x128 at the Commodore 128's own untouched 80-column power-on screen, with
# the CP/M Plus system disk sitting UNBOOTED in drive 8. Nothing is curated into
# the fixture and nothing is typed after the restore — the plus4 lesson applied
# before the mistake rather than after it: put the affordances in the exhibit UI
# around the state the machine itself chose.
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Commodore 128 (PAL) at its own untouched 80-column power-on screen: "COMMODORE BASIC V7.0 122365 BYTES FREE / (C)1986 COMMODORE ELECTRONICS, LTD. / (C)1977 MICROSOFT CORP. / ALL RIGHTS RESERVED / READY." in the VDC's cyan on black, drawn 1:1 (no -VDCdsize) by VICE x128 in a 789x576 window that fills an 800x600 X root. The VDC is a SECOND canvas in VICE's SDL2 build and -80col is what makes it the visible one; -dualwindow never shows it under a kiosk with no window manager. The CP/M 3.0 system disk is in drive 8 but deliberately NOT on the command line - the KERNAL boots any CP/M disk it finds at reset, so the kiosk attaches it ~10 s later over VICE's guest-local text monitor. The visitor reaches CP/M by typing BOOT, which the SPA's c128 on-screen keyboard sends from one labelled button. No C64 button: GO64 works but paints the VIC-II, and with -80col the visible VDC canvas freezes. Keyboard-only exhibit; no pointer device; SID sound -> ALSA -> AC97.

# ---- KEYBOARD PACING (the exhibit's only input surface) ----
# Same emulator, same 50 Hz PAL frame and the same host as vic20/plus4, so the
# same four frames each way. Those numbers were BISECTED on the VIC-20
# (scripts/dev/emu-key-pacing-bisect.py: 40/40 corrupted 1 line in 22, 80/80
# none in 22); the two-frame figure in the playbook is a floor, not an answer.
# The failure they guard against is a host scheduling stall, a property of this
# box rather than of the emulated machine. Re-bisect if this tile ever shows
# dropped characters.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=80
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=80
# No SH_KEY_MAP: VICE's default SDL symbolic keymap already maps host ASCII onto
# the Commodore matrix, and everything this exhibit needs (BOOT, RETURN, the
# BASIC 7.0 keywords) is plain ASCII. The C128's own extra keys - the numeric
# keypad, HELP, 40/80 DISPLAY, ESC - are on the SPA keyboard's overflow row.
